  "id": "secondary-quality",
  "term": "secondary quality",
  "definition": "In this historical usage, a secondary quality is a property understood as arising from how matter acts rather than from a fixed, sharply bounded substance. Here, impenetrability is treated as secondary because it is explained as the increasing repulsive force that prevents two portions of matter from occupying the same space.",
